            "text": "{{Use dmy dates|date=January 2026}}"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Haworthiopsis limifolia, formerly Haworthia limifolia, is a species of flowering plant in the family Asphodelaceae. It is native to southern Africa and first described in 1910."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Distribution\nIt is native to southeastern Africa (southern Mozambique, Swaziland, KwaZulu-Natal, and Mpumalanga)."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p4",
            "text": "Varieties\nIt is a relatively widespread species, with several known varieties, including arcana, gigantea, glaucophylla, keithii, striata, ubomboensis."
          }
        ]
      }
